## Best Practices

### 1. Always Validate Input

```typescript
// Every endpoint should validate
const validation = validateQueryParams(url, [...]);
if (!validation.valid) {
  return validationErrorResponse(validation.errors, requestId);
}
```

### 2. Always Handle Errors

```typescript
// Use try-catch or asyncHandler
try {
  // Your code
} catch (error) {
  return createErrorResponse(error, requestId, path);
}
```

### 3. Always Include CORS

```typescript
import { CORS_HEADERS, createJSONResponse } from '../utils/request';

// Use createJSONResponse (includes CORS automatically)
return createJSONResponse({ data });

// Or manually
headers: { ...CORS_HEADERS }
```

### 4. Always Track Requests

```typescript
import { generateRequestId } from '../utils/request';

// Generate requestId at start
const requestId = generateRequestId();

// Include in response (automatic with createJSONResponse)
return createJSONResponse({ ...data, requestId });
```

### 5. Always Log Appropriately

```typescript
import { createLogger } from '../utils/logger';

const logger = createLogger(request);

// Start of request
logger.info('request_received', { method, path });

// Success
logger.info('query_completed', { recordCount: count });

// Error
logger.error('query_failed', { errorCode: error.code }, error);
```

